==Strategy==
As you can only use [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]], and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]], the only options here are to rely on Uber/Legend Rares and have them carry you through the stage, or instead use highly leveled Normal Cats. Without the right Uber/Legend Rares, a [[Cat Combo]] (or several) may be necessary to assist your Normal units.

The main thing to look out for is the support of the Doge and Roo variants. Wahwah's constant knockback and swift multi-hits allow both himself and his peons to easily waltz up to your base. You will need to find a way to keep the king at bay while lasting long enough that the support begins to dry up in which you can whittle down Wahwah without much worry.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
The following [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] are good for this stage, and if you have any of these, using them will make things easier.

Noting how you will need to focus on 3 traits ([[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]) as well as the limited unit pool to choose from, the Recommended Ubers section will contain Ubers that have been shown to help against a specific trait. [[:Category:Cats with Strong ability|Cats that are Strong]] or [[:Category:Cats with Massive Damage ability|do Massive Damage]] are recommended, as the longer they're at your base, the less room you will have since Wahwah will continuously knock your units back.

'''[[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Anti-Dark]] Ubers:''' [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]], [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]], etc.

'''[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]] Ubers:''' [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bora]], [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]], [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]], etc.

'''[[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie]] Ubers:''' [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]], [[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Sarukani]], [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Thermae D-Lux]] etc.

'''Generalist Ubers:''' Ubers that can either help against more than one trait and/or help against Wahwah.
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]: [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]]/[[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Zombie]] + Zombie Killer, just watch your money.
*[[EVA Unit-01 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-01]]: Another Anti-Alien/Zombie with Zombie Killer, can be used as a substitute or conjunction with Ganglion.
*[[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]]: Universal Strong ability against all traited enemies. Take note that he does not have Zombie Killer and can be a cash sink.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Divine Kai μ's knockback immunity, massive HP and damage, and point-blank range allows her to nearly carry the stage, being able to solo Wahwah without his support. Since the Roos are only singular, she can also be used to get a quick kill on them.
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] Ubers: These units have abilities targeting [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]] and can thus prove effective against King Wahwah himself.

